type: software
title: "tess-transit-times: Mid-Transit Times of Known Planets from TESS Light Curves"
version: 0.5.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23875330
date-released: 2026-11-02
authors:
  - family-names: Stinga
    given-names: Stefano Ivan
    affiliation: Independent researcher
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3860-3944"
    email: stefano@stinga.jp
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sting1JP/tess-transit-times"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Python tool (timing.py) that measures the mid-transit times of a known transiting planet in TESS SPOC 2-min
  or TESS-SPOC full-frame-image light curves. It keeps only transits with complete coverage, fits one
  limb-darkened transit shape to all of them, then fits each mid-time with the shape fixed, with errors scaled
  for excess and red noise. The timing.py in version 0.5.0 is the code used for the TESS transit times of
  WASP-22 b (Stinga 2026, Research Notes of the AAS, 10, 297). It includes a light-curve download helper, an offline
  self-test, a Monte Carlo check of the error bars and the published WASP-22 b times as a known answer.
keywords:
